<title>HUNGARY: HUNGARY'S MKB BANK TAKES UP $50 MLN LOAN.</title>
<headline>HUNGARY'S MKB BANK TAKES UP $50 MLN LOAN.</headline>
<dateline>BUDAPEST 1997-07-11</dateline>
<text>
<p>Hungary's Magyar Kulkereskedelmi Bank Rt (MKB) tapped markets for a $50 million syndicated loan organised by Bankgesellschaft Berlin AG, Hungarian news agency MTI said quoting MKB.</p>
<p>The loan was extended for five years and has interest of 18.5 basis points above LIBOR, it said. The loan will assist MKB's lending activity, it said.</p>
<p>The consortium of lenders included three German banks and a Luxembourg bank, it said.</p>
<p>MKB is majority owned by Germany's Bayerische Landesbank Girozentrale .</p>
<p>-- Budapest newsroom +36 1 327-4040</p>
